## Important Changes in 2026 Guidelines

Several historical contraindications have been **removed or downgraded**: [^1_1][^1_2][^1_3]


| Historical Contraindication | 2026 Status |
| :-- | :-- |
| Advanced age (>80 years) | **No longer a contraindication** |
| Mild or rapidly improving stroke | **Relative** (non-disabling deficits should NOT be thrombolyzed; use DAPT instead) |
| Severe stroke (NIHSS >25) | **Relative** (IVT may benefit if ASPECTS ≥7) |
| History of stroke + diabetes | **No longer absolute** |
| Time window >4.5 hours | **Relative** (IVT with advanced imaging up to 9 hours or wake-up stroke) |
| Single or dual antiplatelet therapy | **NOT a contraindication** (AHA/ASA 2026 Class 1/B-NR) |
| Prior ICH (remote, hypertensive) | **Relative** (individualized decision) |
| Ischemic stroke within 3 months | **Relative** (selected cases) |
| Unruptured aneurysm | **NOT a contraindication** (low risk) |
| Extracranial cervical artery dissection | **Benefit > risk** (IVT reasonable within 4.5 hours) |
| Extra-axial tumors (meningioma) | **Individualized** (generally safe) |
| Sickle cell disease | **IVT safe and effective** (Class 2a) |
| Moya-Moya disease | **IVT likely beneficial** |


